<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συρμ-αία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συρμ-αίη</span></b> , ἡ, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συρμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			) <i>purge-plant</i>, a name given to <i>the radish</i>,
			as used by the Egyptians (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελανοσυρμαῖος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.88
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				125
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1254
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.327
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				1.64
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ συρμαϊσμοῦ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Did.
			</span></i> ap. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i> l.c.:—its juice mixed with salt water they used as
				<i>a purgative and emetic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.78
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a mixture of honey and suet</i>, given as a prize at Sparta, in
			a contest of the same name, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(1).222.7
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">v B.C.</span> ?), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
